{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat docs/design/datom.world.md && rg -n \\\"constant|ns-use-function-const|refusals-are-named\\\" . --glob '\"'!target/**'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"---\ndescription: Core philosophy, foundational axioms, invariants, primitives (tuples, streams, host boundaries), architectural commitments, design principles, code style, and development workflow for datom.world\n---\n\n# DATOM.WORLD ARCHITECTURAL FOUNDATIONS & DEVELOPMENT RULES\n\n## Core Philosophy\n\nEverything is data.\nInterpretation > abstraction.\nExplicit causality > implicit assumptions.\nRestrictions are a feature.\n\n### Foundational Axioms\n\n1. **Everything is a Stream**: Portable I/O and system data flow through append-only streams; hosts may also install explicit local functions that perform direct I/O.\n2. **Interpretation Creates Semantics**: Data is syntax; semantics only emerge through interpretation (one truth, many perspectives).\n   At system scale, a \"system\" is an emergent property of interpreters of\n   pure data, not an object, service, or stored artifact. Find the\n   interpreters and the data they share to find the system.\n3. **Code and State are Datoms**: Code (Universal AST) and runtime execution state are structured datoms, enabling syntax independence and structural reflection.\n4. **Everything is a Continuation**: Computation is modeled as serializable, portable continuations that can pause, travel across streams, and resume anywhere.\n\n## Non-Negotiable Invariants\n\n- Do not introduce hidden global state.\n- Do not introduce implicit control flow.\n- Do not introduce callbacks; every callback is an event on a stream.\n- Do not introduce shared mutable state.\n- Do not collapse interpretation and execution into the same layer.\n- Do not assume graphs: graphs must be constructed explicitly from tuples.\n- Do not lose information (unitarity): streams are append-only and no datom is destroyed, only reinterpreted. The Universal AST is never lost: it is always retrievable wherever code is lowered, by address or by a query over its datoms. Every derived form (semantic vector, native images, indexes) is an interpretation of it and may drop facts only because the AST remains.\n\n## Tuples and Datoms\n\nTuples are elements in an open moduli space, graded by dimension $n$. A tuple can be any dimension/size.\nA datom is the canonical persistent tuple `[e a v t m]` (entity, attribute, value, transaction, metadata). Persistent facts are immutable datoms.\nSource scope belongs to the interpreter, never to an appended tuple slot. Queries keep physical sources as separate db-values and express union or joins explicitly.\n\nSee [`docs/design/datom.md`](./datom.md) for full specification.\n\n## Streams\n\n`dao.stream` is an I/O monad and the system's portable I/O ABI. Functions consume streams and produce streams.\nHosts may install arbitrary local functions, including direct I/O; their availability and migration semantics must be explicit.\nPortable behavior cannot assume them; portable side effects appear as stream emissions. Direct-I/O host modules are explicitly local and non-migratable (owner decision, 2026-10-23).\nStreams are values that can be sent through streams.\nStreams carry whatever values the consumer needs: no datom requirement, no privileged payload shape.\n\nA stream has no privileged reader, and its meaning is not in it. Any number\nof interpreters may observe the same medium, and each constructs its own\nsemantics from the same batches: a `yin.vm` evaluator observing a program\nstream constructs CESK state and executes it; `dao.space.index` observing\nthe very same stream materializes covered indexes, so `dao.space.query/q`\nanswers Datalog over the program as it grows. Neither knows the other\nexists. The medium is their only coupling, and each observer's ignorance of\nthe other is load-bearing: the evaluator never consults an index to run,\nand the index never evaluates a form to index it. This is how axiom 2\nbecomes architecture: one stream, many interpretations, none of them\nthe stream's own.\n\nFunctions can take anything and return anything.\nAgents are functions, closures, or continuations in `yin.vm` that communicate portably with the outside world through `dao.stream`. Portable agent behavior is specified through stream effects; host-local functions may also perform direct I/O.\n\nSee [`docs/design/dao.stream.md`](./dao.stream.md) for full stream specification.\nSee [`docs/design/yin.vm.streams-all-the-way-down.md`](./yin.vm.streams-all-the-way-down.md) for VM architecture.\n\n### Host Boundaries\n\nA host boundary is the dao.stream abstraction boundary; implementations do not add contracts.\n[datom.world.abi.md](./datom.world.abi.md) owns the doctrine, owner rulings, taxonomy, floor and custody rules.\n\n## Architectural Commitments\n\n- **`dao.jing` is syntax, agents are semantics**: the content-addressed encoding stays passive and payload-agnostic.\n- **Macros are stream topology**: an evaluator knows nothing about macro expansion; expansion happens on the syntax side of a medium boundary, upstream of any evaluator.\n- **Peer observers, one stream**: a generic evaluator and `dao.space` independently observe the same stream topic, as described under Streams. This is not a claim about any two consumers regardless of what they consume.\n- **Observers are independent and optional**: nothing requires a medium to have any particular set of consumers. Which observers exist for a stream is a per-composition choice, not a design-time commitment.\n\n## Design Principles\n\nCode quality is measured by malleability: how cheaply can changes adapt without breaking promises?\nStigmergic coordination emerges from sharing data across streams.\n\n**Systems emerge from interpreters of pure data.** Streams are the\ncomposition medium; each interpreter gives the same data a perspective\nwithout collapsing interpretation into execution or owning the truth.\n\n- `dao.space` emerges from `dao.space.index` and `dao.space.query` over\n  ordinary streams.\n- ShiBi capability, metering, and budget emerge from different\n  interpreters over the same tuples; no token object is stored.\n- The four VMs interpret one Universal AST; many syntaxes feed that AST.\n- The semantic AST in `dao.space` is queryable facts projected by the\n  auto-index observer.\n- Client and server are roles in one stigmergic behavior implemented by\n  interpreters, not distinct kinds of nodes.\n\n**Derive, don't persist.** Before adding a tag, slot, or field to any\ncanonical content-hashed structure (an AST grammar, a datom schema, a row\nshape), check whether a correctly scoped Datalog query over\n`dao.space.query/q` can already compute the fact. If it can, it belongs as a\nquery or projection: new persisted structure migrates every downstream\nconsumer and duplicates authority over a fact a query derives fresh. The\nretired `:global` tag in\n[`docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md`](./yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md) is the\ncase study, including the scoping bug that a naive query introduced.\n\nSee [`docs/agents/malleability.md`](../agents/malleability.md) for complete design guidance (cohesion, coupling, bounded complexity, evolution, testing strategy).\nSee [`docs/agents/vocabulary.md`](../agents/vocabulary.md) for domain vocabulary reference (biology, economics, physics, philosophy).\n\n## Code Style\n\n- Prefer simple data over rich types.\n- Prefer total functions over partial ones.\n- Prefer declarative pipelines over imperative logic.\n- Avoid cleverness.\n- Name things after what they do to streams.\n\n## Development Workflow\n\n- Do not invent abstractions that hide streams.\n- Do not suggest mainstream frameworks unless explicitly asked.\n- Do not optimize prematurely.\n- When uncertain, ask at the architectural level, not the implementation level.\n- Explanations should align with Plan 9 / Datomic / Lisp lineage.\n- Program store writes go through `engine/store-put`; any other store write\n  the store-write audit (`test/yin/vm/store_write_audit_test.clj`)\n  detects must be on its allowlist; its docstring states the residual it\n  leaves to review.\n\n### Problem Decomposition\n\nIf a problem appears complex:\n1. Decompose it into streams.\n2. Identify invariants.\n3. Restrict degrees of freedom.\n4. Make causality explicit.\n5. Let structure emerge from constraints.\n\n## Operational & Specialized Guides\n\n- **Advanced Concepts**: See [`docs/agents/advanced-concepts.md`](../agents/advanced-concepts.md) for parallel transport, capability tokens, and entanglement.\n- **Build & Test**: See [`docs/agents/build-n-test.md`](../agents/build-n-test.md) for build, lint, and test commands and TDD guidelines.\n- **Engineering Team Roster**: See [`docs/agents/team.md`](../agents/team.md) for engineering team roles and LLM model assignments.\n- **Agent Delegation**: See [`docs/agents/roles/orchestrator.md`](../agents/roles/orchestrator.md) for collaboration protocols and delegating tasks or reviews through `agy`, `cmd`, `glm`, `deepseek`, and `codex`; each orchestrator session has its own append-only log at `orchestrator-logs/<unix-time-stamp>-<brief-orchestrator-descriptive-name>.md` under the repository root.\n- **Website & Content**: See [`docs/agents/format.md`](../agents/format.md) for `.chp` and `.blog` EDN/Hiccup file specifications.\n./src/cljd/dao/postgraphics/flutter.cljd:115:        ;; screen-space x-scale so strokes stay constant in screen pixels\n./src/cljc/dao/postgraphics/math.cljc:315:   divide stroke widths by this so strokes stay constant in screen pixels\n./src/cljd/dao/postgraphics/flutter/gpu.cljd:309:   shader by binding the 1x1 white texture and a per-op constant vertex\n./public/chp/shibi.chp:125:          \"Cell membranes are constantly bombarded with noise, false signals, and malicious molecules. Nature evolved proven solutions:\"]\n./public/chp/tracking.chp:75:          \"This is what trackers use when you block cookies. Even if your IP address changes constantly, \"\n./public/chp/tracking.chp:251:          \"constantly surveilled, profiled, and manipulated.\"]]])}\n./src/cljd/dao/stream/transit/cljd.cljd:61:  (if (fn? x) x (constantly x)))\n./src/cljc/dao/postgraphics/lowering.cljc:131:    :or {texture-source-valid? (constantly true)}}]\n./src/cljc/dao/postgraphics/lowering.cljc:215:;;   :texture-source-valid?     (default (constantly true))\n./src/dev/jolt_j5_calibrate.clj:58:;; the wrapper's constants (jolt_parser.cpp), checked against\n./src/cljc/dao/data/btree/cursor.cljc:54:   transition does O(1) work bounded by constants: validation advances at\n./public/chp/blog/power-of-restriction-datom-tuple.blog:37:          [:p \"When data structures vary, every system must constantly ask:\"]\n./src/dev/jolt_udp_probe.clj:12:;; -- constants per platform ---------------------------------------------------\n./src/dev/jolt_udp_probe.clj:377:           \"os.arch=\" (System/getProperty \"os.arch\") \"constants=\" (pr-str consts))\n./test/dao/postgraphics/lowering_test.cljc:186:                               {:texture-source-valid? (constantly\n./src/dev/jolt_j0c_parity.clj:19:;;            constant below when it is helper-fabricated (INDENT, DEDENT,\n./src/dev/jolt_j0c_parity.clj:267:            (first-error :line (constantly 0)) #{:validate! :helper-pin-drift}]\n./src/dev/jolt_j0c_parity.clj:275:            (first-error :message (constantly \"\")) #{:first-message}]\n./src/cljc/dao/space/store/fs.cljc:503:               (let [fd (.openSync fs path (bit-or (.. fs -constants -O_RDONLY)\n./src/cljc/dao/space/store/fs.cljc:504:                                                   (.. fs -constants -O_NONBLOCK)))\n./public/chp/blog/yin-vm-ast-chinese-characters.blog:32:           \". The written form (semantics) remains constant. The spoken forms (syntax) vary wildly. The characters are the canonical representation that defines what \\\"Chinese\\\" is.\"]\n./src/cljs/dao/postgraphics/web/canvas.cljs:173:        ;; the screen-space x-scale to keep them constant in screen pixels.\n./src/dev/jolt_j0c_faults.clj:139:  ([label inject call expect] (check label inject call expect (constantly #{})))\n./public/chp/blog/attention-market-critiques.blog:60:           \"This is why subscription models beat pay-per-view: we prefer flat fees to constant mental accounting.\"]\n./src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc:441:;; heap-allocated frame list, so host stack depth is constant however deep\n./src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc:459:   constant host stack.\"\n./src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc:683:   loop, so a source chain of any depth uses constant host stack. Tuples and\n./src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc:916:   constant-stack loop:\n./src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc:1436:   and any other term, a bare symbol included, as the constant it is.\"\n./src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc:1479:  \"Bind sym to val, or check a constant or an already-bound variable against\n./src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc:1484:   is a constant matching that symbol value.\"\n./src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc:1644:   constant. A collection or relation form takes a sequential or a set ret\n./src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc:2195:          ;; a rule call: its arguments are variables, constants or _.\n./src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc:2467:   term rule a bare symbol is a constant, so there it would silently bind\n./src/dev/latte_oracle_tables.clj:34:                     \";; One row per case site: each arm's clause constants, and whether it has a default.\\n\")\n./public/chp/blog/fractal-borders-without-nations.blog:83:          [:p \"But here's what makes it \" [:em \"strange\"] \": \" [:strong \"the attractor's strength is self-reinforcing but also self-limiting\"] \". As more talent flows in, the region becomes more valuable (stronger attraction), but costs also rise (weaker accessibility). The system never reaches equilibrium,it oscillates, with talent flowing in during booms and flowing out during busts, but the strange attractor persists. Silicon Valley, New York finance, London's financial district,these aren't just places. They're \" [:strong \"stable patterns in the flow of economic activity\"] \", attractors that persist across decades despite constant churn of individuals and companies.\"]\n./collab/1793740000000-engineer-p4-e2e-triage.gpt-6-luna.findings.md:3:## Bare constant refusal\n./collab/1793740000000-engineer-p4-e2e-triage.gpt-6-luna.findings.md:5:`constant-node` lowered unresolved unqualified constants in the global\n./collab/1793740000000-engineer-p4-e2e-triage.gpt-6-luna.findings.md:7:lowering refusal into runtime undefined-constant handling, so\n./collab/1793740000000-engineer-p4-e2e-triage.gpt-6-luna.findings.md:8:`refusals-are-named-test` saw no `:yang.php/unsupported` diagnostic. The\n./collab/1793740000000-engineer-p4-e2e-triage.gpt-6-luna.findings.md:9:lowerer now refuses that global bare-name case with `:construct :constant`;\n./collab/1793740000000-engineer-p4-e2e-triage.gpt-6-luna.findings.md:12:Focused verification: `refusals-are-named-test`, 1 test / 22 assertions / 0\n./collab/1793740000000-engineer-p4-e2e-triage.gpt-6-luna.findings.md:26:predates the bare-constant diagnostic fix; ten constant cases now refuse\n./collab/1793740000000-engineer-p4-e2e-triage.gpt-6-luna.findings.md:102:- `bf8c9c20 fix(yang.php): refuse unresolved global constants`\n./src/dev/jolt_ws_probe.clj:595:    (drive! w [ci] (constantly false) 50)\n./src/dev/jolt_ws_probe.clj:698:            (drive! w [ci] (constantly false) 50)\n./src/dev/jolt_ws_probe.clj:880:              [a1 a2] (with-redefs-fn {send-var (scripted-send stuck (constantly :eagain))}\n./src/dev/jolt_ws_probe.clj:894:              [a1 a2] (with-redefs-fn {send-var (scripted-send stuck (constantly :eagain))}\n./src/dev/jolt_ws_probe.clj:926:            (drive! w [ci] (constantly false) 50)\n./src/dev/jolt_ws_probe.clj:1390:                 (with-redefs-fn (cond-> {send-var (scripted-send stuck (constantly :eagain))\n./test/dao/space/query/datomic_execution_test.cljc:242:(deftest native-syntax-depth-is-bounded-by-a-documented-constant\n./test/dao/space/query/datomic_execution_test.cljc:245:    (testing \"the constant is documented data\"\n./test/dao/space/query/datomic_execution_test.cljc:343:  [{:timeout 1000000 ::dq/now-fn (constantly 0)}\n./test/dao/space/query/datomic_execution_test.cljc:345:   {:timeout 1000000 ::dq/max-steps 1000000 ::dq/now-fn (constantly 0)}])\n./src/cljc/dao/stream/ws/rfc6455.cljc:354:               (update-in [:frame :chunks] (constantly [])))\n./src/cljc/dao/jing/dht.cljc:48:  \"The minimum length of a cookie-less request datagram: a constant of wire\n./test/dao/space/query/datomic_test.cljc:329:    (testing \"a selective constant entity stays selective\"\n./src/cljs/datomworld/demo/yin_repl.cljs:47:;; as a local constant instead.\n./src/dev/quick_sharded_test.clj:123:                       (with-redefs [a/scan-index (constantly [])\n./src/dev/quick_sharded_test.clj:124:                                     a/load-subsystems-config (constantly {:subsystems []})\n./src/dev/quick_sharded_test.clj:154:                     (with-redefs [a/scan-index (constantly [])\n./src/dev/quick_sharded_test.clj:155:                                   a/load-subsystems-config (constantly {:subsystems []})\n./public/chp/blog/all-money-is-monopoly-money.blog:114:          [:p \"Why does the \" [:em \"mechanism\"] \" of money injection matter so little compared to the \" [:em \"destination\"] \" of the flow? Physics offers a useful analogy through the concept of \" [:strong \"gauge invariance\"] \". In gauge theory, the specific choice of gauge (reference frame or unit of measurement) is arbitrary. What matters are the relationships and transformations that remain constant across different gauges. Consider the economy itself: whether transactions occur in dollars, euros, or Bitcoin, the \" [:strong \"actual economic output of goods and services remains the same\"] \". A skilled engineer builds the same bridge, a farmer grows the same crops, a teacher educates the same students. The real productive work is gauge-invariant. What changes across monetary gauges is merely the \" [:em \"accounting representation\"] \" of that work, not the work itself. Similarly, \" [:strong \"how money enters the system is just a choice of gauge\"] \". Whether a dollar flows in through 'efficient' government allocation or 'wasteful' spending or even corruption, the economic reality that matters is \" [:em \"where that dollar flows afterward\"] \": the transformation through productive human capital. The gauge (spending mechanism) is arbitrary; the transformation (flow through skilled networks) is what generates measurable wealth.\"]\n./public/chp/blog/all-money-is-monopoly-money.blog:163:         [:p \"The problem is \" [:strong \"this is not practically achievable\"] \". Not everyone in the U.S. is capable of working in high-tech intellectual fields, nor should they be expected to. People have different aptitudes, interests, and abilities. This problem is compounded by national borders that prevent people from moving to places where work matches their skill level. A software engineer in Lagos cannot simply relocate to Silicon Valley; a factory worker in Ohio cannot move to Shenzhen where manufacturing jobs exist. \" [:strong \"Borders create artificial friction in the global labor market\"] \", trapping people in economies mismatched to their abilities while preventing the natural flow of human capital to where it would be most productive. A functioning economy needs workers at all levels of the fractal structure: skilled machinists, experienced factory workers, customer service representatives who understand complex products, technicians who maintain equipment. \" [:strong \"When you hollow out the middle and lower branches of the fractal tree, the upper branches cannot survive\"] \". The Nobel Prize-winning physicist still depends on the skilled machinist who can fabricate the experimental apparatus, the technician who maintains the equipment, the engineer who understands manufacturing constraints. \" [:strong \"Innovation doesn't happen in isolated intellectual towers\"] \". It emerges from the constant feedback between theoretical insight and practical implementation, between high-level design and hands-on problem-solving. When you sever this connection through outsourcing, even the specialized high-tech sectors eventually atrophy because they lose the grounding in physical reality that drives breakthrough innovation.\"]\n./src/cljs/datomworld/demo/continuation_stream.cljs:404:  {:mount (constantly {:event :compile}),\n./src/cljs/datomworld/demo/continuation_stream.cljs:405:   :unmount (constantly {:event :unmount}),\n./src/cljs/datomworld/demo/continuation_stream.cljs:406:   :compile (constantly {:event :compile}),\n./src/cljs/datomworld/demo/continuation_stream.cljs:407:   :reset (constantly {:event :reset}),\n./src/cljs/datomworld/demo/continuation_stream.cljs:408:   :step (constantly {:event :step}),\n./src/cljs/datomworld/demo/continuation_stream.cljs:409:   :toggle-run (constantly {:event :toggle-run}),\n./test/dao/space/query/execution_test.cljc:115:  (let [at (fn [t] (ex/fn-driver (constantly t)))\n./test/dao/space/query/execution_test.cljc:287:    (let [driver (ex/fn-driver (constantly 101))\n./test/dao/space/query/execution_test.cljc:705:          (run-q {:deadline 100} (ex/fn-driver (constantly 0))\n./public/chp/blog/datoms-as-streams.blog:41:            \"(def datoms\\n  [{:e 1 :a :entity/type :v :person :tx 1001 :c :alpha}\\n   {:e 1 :a :person/name :v \\\"Ada\\\" :tx 1001 :c :alpha}\\n   {:e 2 :a :entity/type :v :device :tx 1002 :c :beta}\\n   {:e 2 :a :device/os :v :ios :tx 1002 :c :beta}])\\n\\n(def entity-types\\n  (materialize-snapshot datoms))\\n\\n(def assertion-count\\n  (transduce (map (constantly 1)) + datoms))\"]]\n./collab/1793515000000-engineer-p4-leak-fix.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md:303:`yang.php.antlr.e2e-test/refusals-are-named-test` (`e2e_test.clj:103-104`),\n./collab/1793515000000-engineer-p4-leak-fix.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md:305:`:yang.php/unsupported` with construct `:constant`, but get no such diagnostic.\n./src/cljc/dao/stream/forward.cljc:33:  ;; Keep dispatch scalar: ClojureDart cannot compile hashed vector constants\n./test/dao/space/query_rules_test.cljc:190:    (testing \"a constant argument\"\n./collab/1793660000000-engineer-p4-yangcall-conformance.gpt-6-luna.findings.md:17:The PHP e2e namespace run excluding `:slow` tests completed with 19 tests, 1,111 assertions, 3 failures, and 0 errors. The two new conformance tests passed. Existing failures were the quick php-src selection (271 entries: 108 pass, 48 unsupported, 115 fail) and two expectations in `refusals-are-named-test` for `<?php echo FOO;` (missing diagnostic). An earlier unfiltered run, started before the closure entry change, also reported the `Zend/tests/gc_023.phpt` slow stress case failing and was stopped before completion.\n./test/dao/space/query_numeric_test.cljc:117:(deftest constant-patterns-match-kind-strictly-through-the-index\n./orchestrator-logs/1793187400000-glm-yang-clojure-hardening.md:22:   elements evaluate (constant-form?/compile-constructed-collection); empty\n./orchestrator-logs/1793192500000-glm-resume-yang-clojure-hardening.md:69:Done: (1) Gate S spec authored by fable (410-line deliverable, collab/1793209191216-architect-gate-s-spec.*), transcribed verbatim to docs/design/yin.cic.spec.md. The sign-off round found FOUR defects in the architect's own content (cross-reference §5.3->§4.3 C-7; B-6 Lean cell was BACKWARDS — under impredicativity Lean accepts the theorem since T:Sort 0, so the recorded boundary pair must be Accept; B-5 prediction replaced with to-be-measured per the methodology's no-unmeasured-predictions rule; A.2 imax/max condition made precise via L-3 normal-form atoms). A