 a spec extension that must arrive together with its termination policy.\n./docs/design/yin.cic.spec.md:231:**Rule C-7 (no self or forward reference).** While checking declaration `d`, the environment is the prefix of `E` strictly before `d`. A `const` naming `d` itself or any later declaration is Reject (R-CONST, `:unknown-constant`).\n./docs/design/yin.cic.spec.md:235:**Rule C-8.** `t ⇝ u` is the result of applying C-1 to C-4 at the head of `t` until no rule applies. The head positions are: the term itself, and the function position of an `app`. Reduction under `lam`, `pi`, `let` binders and in argument positions is not part of whnf. Delta (C-4) applies at the head only when no C-1 to C-3 step applies, and only when the constant is in head position of an application spine or is the term itself. The order of application does not affect the result because the system is confluent on well-typed terms; the implementation may choose any order.\n./docs/design/yin.cic.spec.md:239:**Rule C-9.** `E; Γ ⊢ t ≡ u` is the least relation that is reflexive by T-3, symmetric, transitive, closed under C-1 to C-4 in any position, and a congruence for every constructor, with sorts compared by L-4 and constants compared by name and L-4 on their level lists.\n./docs/design/yin.cic.spec.md:259:**Example C-d.** Same as C-c but `id` admitted as a `theorem`: Reject (C-9). The constant is opaque, both whnfs are the application spine itself, and `const h []` is not an application. This is boundary fixture B-5.\n./docs/design/yin.cic.spec.md:294:**Rule D-5 (axiom).** `E; ps; · ⊢ T type` and `c` is in the admitted-axiom list of the checking configuration ⟹ `E ⊢ axiom c [ps] T admissible`. An axiom outside the admitted list is Reject (D-5, `:axiom-not-admitted`). An axiom is never marked proved, is never unfolded, and every `Accept` of a declaration reports the set of axioms in its transitive constant closure.\n./docs/design/yin.cic.spec.md:305:**Example D-d.** `definition loop [] (sort zero) (const loop [])` into `·`: Reject (R-CONST, `:unknown-constant`) by C-7.\n./docs/design/yin.cic.spec.md:321:**Rule X-5 (no proof irrelevance).** With axioms `P : sort zero`, `h₁ : const P []`, `h₂ : const P []`: `const h₁ [] ≡ const h₂ []`: Reject (C-9). Different opaque constants are not convertible.\n./docs/design/yin.cic.spec.md:364:| B-5 | unfolding of a `theorem` constant, Example C-d | Reject (C-9) | to be measured against the pinned oracle before the fixture is recorded; no prediction is made here |\n./test/yin/repl/query_test.cljc:241:(deftest a-bare-symbol-in-a-pattern-is-the-symbol-constant\n./docs/design/dao.space.schema.md:200:any other tuples — never a code-level constant. The interpreter's code\n./src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:97:   \"classConstant\" :class-constant})\n./src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:271:;; Literals and constants\n./src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:301:(defn- numeric-constant\n./src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:323:(defn- builtin-constant-node\n./src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:324:  \"The literal node of builtin constant value `v` (`builtins/constants`).\"\n./src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:412:        ;; `namespace A;` parses as an expression statement over the constant\n./src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:418:                          c (when (and e (= 1 (count (core/kids ctx e)))) (first (core/rules ctx e \"constant\")))\n./src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:522:   constant (:const) name: an import wins, an unqualified name inside a\n./src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:546:(defn- constant-node\n./src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:547:  \"The node of a read of constant `q` (parts of its written name). A builtin\n./src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:555:      (contains? builtins/constants primary) (builtin-constant-node (get builtins/constants primary))\n./src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:557:      ;; constant declarations are statically resolved, accepting one here\n./src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:558:   