n and review artifacts, including the runtime fallback-guard adjudication.\\nI have read all four slice implementation and review reports. Before inspecting the git branch state, contract doc, and source/test diffs on `datomic-q-4b-ci`, I will briefly review [malleability.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/agents/malleability.md) as referenced by the Lead System Architect role definition.\\nI will now inspect the git repository state and commit history between `master` and `datomic-q-4b-ci` to see all files touched by Phase 4b and check what branch the working tree currently points to.\\nThe working tree is on `master` while Phase 4b is committed on `datomic-q-4b-ci` (`301041471231a748cc24ecc40bff508a18e6b8db`, 16 files changed). Keeping the working tree untouched, I will inspect the branch files directly via `git show` and `git diff`, starting with `cursor.cljc`, `storage.cljc`, and `execution.cljc`.\\nI will read `dao.data.btree` around `descend-from`, `advance`, and `slice*` to compare the cursor's seek/advance state machine against the reference B-tree implementation, and also inspect the diffs in `query.cljc`, `datomic.cljc`, `cljd_agg.clj`, and the compatibility contract.\\nI will now inspect the full `query.cljc`, `datomic.cljc`, and `dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md` on `datomic-q-4b-ci` to trace every read path, realization hop, planner check, error mapping, and contract clause.\\nI have read all source and contract changes across `cursor.cljc`, `storage.cljc`, `execution.cljc`, `query.cljc`, `datomic.cljc`, `cljd_agg.clj`, and `dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md`. Next, I will read the four new test suites on `datomic-q-4b-ci` (`cursor_test.cljc`, `storage_read_test.cljc`, `published_read_test.cljc`, and `published_bounded_test.cljc`) to verify test coverage and instrumentation methodology.\\nI have finished reading the four new test suites. Next, I will inspect `src/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc` (to cross-check `read-manifest`, `compare-vals`, and index comparators against `valid-read-descriptor?`, `range-plan`, and `cursor.cljc`) and check the recent gate reproduction entry in [orchestrator-log.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/orchestrator-log.md).\\nI noticed `master` has advanced past `datomic-q-4b-ci~1` and that `orchestrator-log.md` mentions a Jolt test-manifest check. I will inspect the commits on `master` since `datomic-q-4b-ci` branched to check for merge/manifest interactions, as well as the surrounding contract sections in `dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md`.\\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-10-25 16:46:17 GMT\\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-25 23:46:17 +07\\nCoding-Agent: agy\\nSession-ID: c1fe6b10-09b2-45c8-8553-7138aab37a1e\\n\\n# Architect Sign-Off: Phase 4b Checked Published-Index Traversal (`datomic-q-4b-ci` @ `30104147`)\\n\\n- **Role**: Lead System Architect (`Gemini 4 Argon`, family-independent alternate architect seat per [architect.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/agents/roles/architect.md))\\n- **Prompt**: [1792931003000-architect-datomic-q-phase4b-signoff.prompt.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792931003000-architect-datomic-q-phase4b-signoff.prompt.md)\\n- **Written Rulings**: [`r7` seam design](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792931003000-architect-datomic-q-phase4b-seam-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md) + [`r8` revision](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792931003000-architect-datomic-q-phase4b-design-r2.gpt-6-astra.findings.md) (`r8` supersedes conflicting `r7` text)\\n- **Target Branch**: `datomic-q-4b-ci` (`301041471231a748cc24ecc40bff508a18e6b8db`, cleanly branched from `9968d37f` with zero file overlap against current `master` `6155aa95`)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Conformance to the `r7` + `r8` Written Design\\n\\nThe implemented seam conforms to the `r7` + `r8` written design across all layers and upholds all six non-negotiable invariants of [datom.world.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/datom.world.md) (explicit immutable state, explicit control flow, pull-based step cursors without callbacks, zero shared mutable query state, strict layer separation, and explicit relational/view values).\\n\\n### Verified Design Invariants\\n- **Pure Stepped Cursor ([cursor.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/data/btree/cursor.cljc))**: Zero `:require` dependencies and zero I/O, storage handles, clocks, or execution state. Public API matches `r8` exactly: [`start`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/data/btree/cursor.cljc#L127-L162) pins `comparator` (`::cmp`); [`step`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/data/btree/cursor.cljc#L375-L390) performs one constant-bounded local transition returning `:continue`, `:need-node`, `:item`, or `:done`; [`supply`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/data/btree/cursor.cljc#L165-L194) satisfies at most one pending request and rejects unsolicited (`:unexpected-response`), wrong-address (`:address-mismatch`), and duplicate (`:already-satisfied`) responses. Empty trees (`count == 0` / `root == nil`) step directly to `:done` without issuing a read; waiting cursors (`:awaiting`) re-step idempotently to the same `:need-node`. Every step does bounded work: [`check-shape!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/data/btree/cursor.cljc#L228-L257) is $O(1)$, [`validate-step`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/data/btree/cursor.cljc#L260-L290) checks at most `validation-chunk = 32` keys per `:continue`, [`first-ge`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/data/btree/cursor.cljc#L197-L208) binary-searches within one node, [`advance-step`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/data/btree/cursor.cljc#L357-L372) pops one exhausted branch frame per transition, and [`enter-step`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/data/btree/cursor.cljc#L293-L328) + [`yield-step`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/data/btree/cursor.cljc#L331-L354) match [`slice*`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/data/btree.cljc#L1940-L1955) on inclusive/exclusive bounds and comparator-equal child maxima (`(zero? (cmp ... sep))`). Occupancy/branching-factor fill validation is absent per `r8` F1.\\n- **Single-Node Reader \\u0026 Open-Time Descriptor**: [`read-node-blob`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/data/btree/storage.cljc#L48-L59) executes exactly one hash-verifying `jing/get`, throws `\\\"missing index segment\\\"` on miss, and leaves `KVStorage/-restore` untouched on the checked path; the stale `:verify?` docstring in [storage.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/data/btree/storage.cljc#L10-L20) is corrected. [`published-db`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L235-L254) attaches `:dao.space.query/published-read {:version 1 :store :manifest-address :manifest}` from the already-read manifest (zero extra fetches), and [`open-published!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L257-L295) preserves it without changing the persistent coordinate or handle ownership.\\n- **Admission Table**: [`source-step`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L580-L612) is shared by adapter pre-flight ([`source-admissible?`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/query/datomic.cljc#L590-L610) / [`check-bounded-sources!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/query/datomic.cljc#L612-L628)) and bounded core realization ([`realize-st`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L662-L675) -\\u003e [`realize-checked-st`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L615-L627)). All declared `:in` db sources (including unused ones) are checked iteratively before evaluation; only materialized sources/views and depth-0 `current` (no `:as-of`, no `history`, no nested views) over a published value with a structurally valid descriptor ([`valid-read-descriptor?`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L563-L578)) are admitted. `:rows` is never forced and restored `BTSet`s are never consulted on the checked path.\\n- **Sentinels, Tie-Scanning, and Single Kernel**: [`range-plan`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L789-L817) uses the exact `r8` canonical `[e a v t m]` sentinels (`[e nil nil nil nil]`, `[nil a nil nil nil]`, `[nil a v nil nil]`, `[nil nil v nil nil]`, `nil` for full EAVT walk), never manufactures a nil-padded upper key, continues across comparator-tied values via [`same-slot?`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L755-L762), and applies kind-strict `cbor/content=` filtering afterward via [`slot-pred`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L776-L782). [`datoms-st`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L845-L857) routes pattern scans, full-EAVT fallback, joins, flat/nested/wildcard pull (including `(pull ?e pattern)` in `:find`), `get-else`/`missing?`, `not`/`not-join` (preserving `reduced` first-witness stop), `or`/`or-join`, rules, and aggregates through the existing single trampoline evaluator. Unbounded calls (`restored-datoms-st`, `select-by-index`, `rows`, `match`, `pull`) keep their pre-existing restored-tree / memoized behavior untouched.\\n- **One-In-Flight Guarantee \\u0026 Accounting**: [execution.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/query/execution.cljc#L56-L77) adds `:tree-step 1`, `:node-read 1`, and phase `:read` while staying storage- and syntax-free. [`checked-datoms-st`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L895-L970) charges `:tree-step` before every `cursor/step`, charges `:node-read` before each [`read-step`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/query/execution.cljc#L190-L206) wrapping one `read-node-blob`, discards any post-expiry blob without calling `cursor/supply`, and preserves read/corruption exceptions as `:source-failed` (never swallowing a failed read into `:timeout`).\\n\\n### Cited Deviations from `r7` + `r8` (All Non-Blocking)\\n1. **Runtime fallback guard in core vs. static clause refusal at adapter** (`r7` §6/§9): Deliberate architecture split adjudicated in 4b-3/4b-4 — evaluated and confirmed in §2 below.\\n2. **Added cross-leaf strictly-increasing key check ([`yield-step`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/data/btree/cursor.cljc#L340-L343))**: Beyond `r8`'s intra-node ordering + parent-separator check, the cursor also rejects `(not (pos? (cmp k last-key)))` across consecutive yielded items across leaf boundaries. Sound for `dao.data.btree` sorted sets (which deduplicate comparator-equal full keys; documented in [cursor.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/data/btree/cursor.cljc#L64-L71)).\\n3. **Single-slot `::satisfied` memory ([`supply`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/data/btree/cursor.cljc#L158-L177))**: Retains only the most recently satisfied address rather than a history set; re-supplying an *older* satisfied address while idle rejects with `:unexpected-response` instead of `:already-satisfied` (both reject; documented at [cursor.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/data/btree/cursor.cljc#L37-L40)).\\n4. **Structural descriptor slack vs. [`valid-manifest?`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc#L286-L303)**: [`valid-read-descriptor?`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L563-L578) checks `(integer? count)`, `(integer? branching-factor)`, and `(map? indexes)` without checking `(not (neg? count))` or key-set completeness of `:indexes`; [`start`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/data/btree/cursor.cljc#L131-L146) catches inconsistent `count`/`root` (wrapped in `guarded` -\\u003e `:source-failed` with zero reads when scanned, though an *unused* forged descriptor with negative `:count` passes admission). Unreachable via `published-db`/`open-published!` since `read-manifest` enforces `valid-manifest?`. Similarly, `cursor/start` ignores `:branching-factor` values (consistent with `r8` F1) and treats bound `:inclusive?` by truthiness rather than strict `boolean?`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Runtime-Fallback-Guard Adjudication\\n\\n**CONFIRMED.**\\n\\nInspection of the call graph verifies that [`resolve-relation`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L1544-L1553) has a single caller in the evaluator: the non-3-slot / `\\u0026`-rest fallback arm of [`emit-pattern`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L1803-L1832).\\n1. **At the binding Client adapter profile ([datomic.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/query/datomic.cljc))**: [`translate-clauses`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/query/datomic.cljc#L283-L315) and [`translate-rules`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/query/datomic.cljc#L317-L339) pass every `:where` clause (including nested `not`/`not-join`/`or`/`or-join`/`and`) and every `%` rule body through [`pad-pattern`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/query/datomic.cljc#L262-L280) *before* [`q-with-state`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2364-L2420) runs. `pad-pattern` statically rejects empty, $\\u003e3$-slot, and `\\u0026`-rest tuple patterns and normalizes 1–3 slots to 3 fixed slots. Because a realized checked source always populates `::fact-index` (`{::checked ...}`), `emit-pattern` always takes [`datoms-st`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L1810) and can never reach `resolve-relation` through `datomic/q`. Thus **refuse-before-any-read holds unconditionally on the public contract surface**.\\n2. **At internal core `q-with-state`**: Throwing `{:reason :checked-source-fallback}` inside `resolve-relation` enforces the hard invariant (zero eager fallback to `force-relation` / `:rows`) without duplicating recursive rule-body syntax analysis in core for non-Client tuple shapes, and the distinction is explicitly disclosed under *Adapter-profile boundary* in [dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md#L648-L658).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Defects Missed by the Review Chain\\n\\n**No blocking architectural defects found.** Independent line-by-line review of [cursor.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/data/btree/cursor.cljc) and the [query.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc) / [datomic.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/query/datomic.cljc) / [cljd_agg.clj](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/cljd_agg.clj) diffs surfaced four non-blocking (P3) items missed across slices 4b-1..4b-4:\\n\\n1. **P3 — Unguarded datom-slot inspection after `:item` / `:done` in [`checked-datoms-st`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L924-L968)**: `cursor/start`, `cursor/step`, `cursor/supply`, and `bts/read-node-blob` are wrapped in [`guarded`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L888-L892) (`::source-failure` -\\u003e `:source-failed`), but `(continue? d)` (`:961`), `(pred d)` (`:966`), and `(current-state-seq kept)` in `finish` (`:927`) are not. Because `cursor.cljc` is deliberately key-agnostic and only invokes `cmp` when `cnt \\u003e= 2`, `lower != nil`, or `last-key` is populated:\\n   - A poisoned single-key leaf holding a non-datom (e.g., `{:keys [42]}`) under an unselective full-EAVT scan (`lower = nil`) passes `cursor/step` with zero comparator calls and throws `UnsupportedOperationException` / `IndexOutOfBoundsException` in `current-state-seq`, which [`classify-core-failure`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/query/datomic.cljc#L541-L565) maps to `:evaluation-failed` instead of `:source-failed` (still `:cognitect.anomalies/fault`, cause preserved, zero leaks).\\n   - A poisoned leaf holding conflicting d5 history (same `[e a v t]`, distinct `m`, which `eavt-cmp` orders strictly) throws `\\\"conflicting d5 rows: same [e a v t], different m\\\"` (`ex-data` `{:a ... :b ...}`) in [`current-state-seq`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L109-L114), which `classify-core-failure` (`:560-564`) strips and classifies as `:invalid-request` rather than `:source-failed`.\\n   - *Why non-blocking*: Unreachable for any `publish-index!` output (enforced by [`local-datom?`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/datom.cljc#L42-L57) at publish time and hash-verified by `jing/get`); neither leaks state/datoms nor violates one-in-flight bounds. Follow-up: wrap `continue?`, `pred`, and `current-state-seq` in `guarded` inside `checked-datoms-st`.\\n2. **P3 — Stale Phase 4a docstrings and refusal message**: [execution.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/query/execution.cljc#L23-L28), [datomic.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/query/datomic.cljc#L23-L27), [`realize-st`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L668-L669), and the `:bounded-source-unqualified` message in [`check-bounded-sources!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/query/datomic.cljc#L621-L624) (`\\\"bounded execution requires an explicit materialized relation source\\\"`) still state that bounded calls admit only materialized sources.\\n3. **P3 — Public helper in dev tooling**: [`jvm-only?`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/cljd_agg.clj#L83-L89) is `defn` rather than `defn-` with no external callers (per [malleability.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/agents/malleability.md) surface-area discipline).\\n4. **Operational Merge Note — Jolt J2 test-manifest registration**: [subsystems.edn](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/subsystems.edn) needs no update (`dao.data` and `dao.space` prefixes cover all new namespaces), and `datomic-q-4b-ci` merges cleanly onto `master`. However, [`check-manifest!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj#L325-L360) in [jolt_j2_lane.clj](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj) requires every `*_test.cljc` under `test/dao/{data,space}` to be listed in `included` or `excluded`. Post-merge, register the four new portable `.cljc` suites (`dao.data.btree.cursor-test`, `dao.data.btree.storage-read-test`, `dao.space.published-read-test`, `dao.space.query.published-bounded-test`) in `jolt_j2_lane.clj` so `bb test:jolt-j2` stays green.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. Fidelity of the Contract's Phase 4b Amendment Text\\n\\nThe Phase 4b amendments in [dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md) are a **faithful record** of both the `r7` + `r8` rulings and the shipped implementation:\\n- Status header (`:1-16`), `:tree-step` / `:node-read` step-unit calibration (`:35-65` — 32-key validation chunks, no universal $2\\\\times$ conversion, cold-scan repeat charges), unchanged *Storage checkpoints and overshoot* (`:72-82`), `:read` phase-of-death note (`:440-443`), updated *Staged source qualification* (`:563-582`), exact §9 admission table (`:587-604`), cursor/reader/descriptor/interpreter mechanism (`:607-646`), canonical-slot sentinel table and `same-slot?` + `cbor/content=` rule (`:660-683`), memoization ownership clarification (`:641-646`), *Adapter-profile boundary* (`:648-658`), three-host evidence (`:1007-1052`), and effort table (`:1087`) all match `r7` + `r8` and the code.\\n- **Two minor P3 doc-polish notes** for a future pass:\\n  1. The validation bullet ([dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md#L623-L628)) mentions intra-node strict ordering and child-maximum separator equality, omitting the extra cross-leaf strictly-increasing check in [`yield-step`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/data/btree/cursor.cljc#L340-L343).\\n  2. Under *Sizing and read observability*, a pre-4b baseline sentence ([dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md#L794-L796)) still cites `(seq (:eavt idx))` at baseline `query.cljc:526` without noting that bounded checked sources now execute that unselective full-EAVT walk through `dao.data.btree.cursor` (the sizing warning itself remains accurate).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Unverified\\n\\n- **Local test execution**: Not re-run locally in this sandboxed headless session (JDK is managed under `~/.local` via `mise` outside sandbox read paths); sign-off relies on full static verification of all 16 changed/added files on `datomic-q-4b-ci` (`30104147`) paired with the orchestrator's clean remote reproduction on `jupiter` (`bb test:sub dao.data dao.space` -\\u003e `clj` 27ns/560/0, `cljs` 26/550/0, `cljd` 26/550/0; `clj-kondo` 0/0).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. Sign-Off Verdict\\n\\nSIGNED OFF\\n\",\"duration_seconds\":828.746711,\"num_turns\":1,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":346043,\"output_tokens\":35418,\"thinking_tokens\":21511,\"cache_read_tokens\":3524417,\"total_tokens\":381461}}\n./archive/yin-ucf/1790851062697-vm-engineer-d7-host-typed-closures.orchestrator-cljd-r3.log:501:\r02:52 +727: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-d7/test/cljd-out/yin/vm/host-typed-values-test_test.dart: null yin.vm.host-typed-values-test/guest-printing-of-a-closure-is-opaque-test                    \r02:52 +728: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-d7/test/cljd-out/yin/vm/host-typed-values-test_test.dart: null yin.vm.host-typed-values-test/guest-printing-of-a-closure-is-opaque-te