at the expression editor uses X11 for the clipboard supported by the Chez source at c/expeditor.c:1189-1212 in the mise-installed or downloaded tarball, e.g. under ~/.local/share/mise/downloads/chezscheme-10.4.1/ or the extracted sources you can find; are --disable-x11 and --disable-curses really configure options in that source); (b) is the package name right for the Debian family (libx11-dev on Debian/Ubuntu); is anything else the Chez source build includes that the same machine lacked (grep the jupiter log for other missing headers/libraries; note that the first jupiter failure list had only X11); (c) does the declaration stay consistent with the file's conventions (comment style, the :unverified entries incl. the already-corrected libssl3 note); (d) one-entry change, no other file touched; (e) honest description in the commit message. Under 300 words, final response only, header fields, verdict SIGNED OFF / SIGNED OFF WITH CHANGES / NOT SIGNED OFF, findings table (id, severity, file:line, evidence, correction), and what you could not verify.\"}],\"meta\":{\"source\":\"user\",\"createdAt\":1792519675776,\"messageId\":\"65e24b91-6edf-4157-9ee1-fd23b340349c\"}},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"Cannot execute git commands (shell is blocked). I need to read jolt-toolchain.edn in the worktree (the committed state should match), grep for errors in the jupiter logs, and check the Chez source in the mise download for c/expeditor.c:1189-1212 and the configure options.\\n\\nSteps:\\n1. Read jolt-toolchain.edn in the jolt-j0a worktree (os-packages section).\\n2. Grep for X11/expeditor errors in jupiter-mise-install.log.\\n3. Look for the Chez source: ~/.local/share/mise/downloads/chezscheme-10.4.1/ — search with Glob. The workspace root is /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld; the home directory is outside the workspace — can read_file read files outside the workspace? \\\"Must be within the workspace (current directory or its additional