ng REPL composition can reach, it is committed and\\n476: regenerated by the tool, and a file no `src` namespace requires cannot\\n477: affect a host's behaviour until something requires it, at which point it\\n478: enters the closure and the gate sees it. The five out-of-closure sites are\\n479: recorded for the deferred design (§9.1) as reachable only from tests or\\n480: not at all. The 21: `dao/stream/ringbuffer.cljc:27,185`; `memory_log.cljc:73`;\\n481: `ws.cljc:122`; `remote.cljc:1249`; `remote_pair.cljc:180`;\\n482: `remote_route.cljc:173`; `journal.cljc:296`; `dao/jing/content/step.cljc:132`;\\n483: `dao/lease.cljc:594`; `dao/space/store/fs.cljc:137,351`;\\n484: `yin/vm/linker.cljc:1685`; `yin/vm/ucf/custody.cljc:46`;\\n485: `yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver.cljc:1507`; `yin/vm/telemetry.cljc:112`;\\n486: `yin/repl.cljc:667,668,733,918`; `yin/repl/dht.cljc:117`.\\n487: \\n488: Other sources, as the H0 gate resolves them (V): `rand` at\\n489: `rpc.cljc:114-116`, `rand-int` at `jing/dht.cljc:373`; secure generators at\\n490: `space/dht.cljc:142-151` and `sign.cljc:119-123`, plus `sign.cljc:79`, the\\n491: deterministic seed-replay proxy, which matches by name and sits in list 2's\\n492: ceiling for that file with a comment (§2.5 rules it internal); `gensym` at\\n493: three sites; clocks at `main.cljc:1242,1275,1408,1435,1542` (driver),\\n494: `driver.clj:169,206` (JVM lane) and the three ws seams (`ws/jvm.clj:422`,\\n495: `ws/node.cljs:249`, `ws/dart.cljd:176`, seam-private); ambient at\\n496: `fs.cljc:92,136,271-273`, `repl.cljc:275-277`, `main.cljc`; printing at\\n497: `main.cljc`: **13 resolved calls** (`println`, `print`, `flush`,\\n498: `js/console.log`; r3's \\\"19\\\" counted lines by text, including `*out*`\\n499: mentions and docstrings, and is withdrawn); `antlr/repl.cljc:71` is not a\\n500: host call (§3.1). Timers the gate sees: `driver.clj:173` (`Thread/sleep`),\\n501: `datagram/jvm.clj:70` and the three waitset drivers; `storage.cljc:224-227`\\n502: is a