image, old writer against new, JVM and Node.       | unchanged; the measurement in the slice report, no threshold      |\\n817: |       |        |                                                                                | (OQ7). Slow tier once after landing.                              |\\n818: +-------+--------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------+\\n819: \\n820: Dependencies: H0, H1, H2 in order; H3 and H4 after H2, in either order.\\n821: \\n822: ### 8.1 List 1: the files permitted non-exempt host arms, baseline and final\\n823: \\n824: The gate never promises \\\"no arms across `src/cljc`\\\", only \\\"no non-exempt\\n825: arms outside list 1\\\". List 1 is generated at H0 by the gate from the actual\\n826: closure (every closure file holding a non-exempt arm, §3.3) and must equal\\n827: the **H0 baseline** below, by category, with each file's reason; a\\n828: difference either way is an H0 finding to resolve before H1. The baseline\\n829: is today's tree: the seven `dao.host.*` files are **planned additions**\\n830: (five in H1, two in H3) and are not part of the H0 baseline; they are\\n831: marked as such in the table.\\n832: \\n833: +----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\\n834: | Category (reason)          | Files (V, from §1 and the closure)                                                              | After H4                    |\\n835: +============================+=================================================================================================+=============================+\\n836: | H1-H4 migration sources    | `yin/vm/integer/host.cljc`, `dao/jing/cbor.cljc`, `dao/jing/cbor/boring.cljc`,                  | Removed from list 1 as each |\\n837: |                            | `src/cljd/dao/jing/cbor/cljd