f0c1b\"}},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"tool_use_id\":\"call_fde29d4ab40647258661bfb5\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Read 1/1 file, 180 lines\\nNote: showing lines 884-1063. More of the file remains. Use offset=1064 to continue.\\n884: files (five in H1, two in H3), which join list 1 when their slices land. The deletions are\\n885: three: `yin/vm/integer/host.cljc` (H2), `dao/jing/cbor/boring.cljc` (H4, the\\n886: JVM/JS Boring wrapper) and `src/cljd/dao/jing/cbor/cljd.cljd` (H4, the Dart\\n887: Jing writer, a lane-specific file that the seams row excludes and the first\\n888: row lists, so that the lane-specific category cannot silently retain it).\\n889: The final list 1 after H4 is therefore: the baseline minus the first row\\n890: (except `sign.cljc` for `generate`), both deleted Jing writers included in\\n891: that subtraction, plus the seven profile files. The host-library gate of\\n892: §8.2 is consistent with it.\\n893: \\n894: **Reconciliation with H0's measurement (r7, V).** H0 generated list 1 as\\n895: 76 files: 60 matching the rows above after the corrections now in them,\\n896: plus 16 tagged `:h0-unlisted`. The 16 are now categorised: nine in the\\n897: first row (profile consumers, H2), six in the \\\"dialect arms\\\" row\\n898: (retained), one (`rpc.cljc`) in the deferred row. **What H0 must change**:\\n899: retag those 16 entries in the gate's list 1 and in the committed closure\\n900: class tags from `:h0-unlisted` to the row above (`:migration-source`,\\n901: `:dialect-arm`, `:deferred-scope`), a data change to the test and the edn\\n902: outputs, no tool change; drop nothing (the six names H0 could not find were\\n903: never on the generated list, and the rows above no longer name them).\\n904: **What H0 need not change**: the totals 142/140/141 and 133 shared stand;\\n905: the traversal, its independent agreement, the two negative tests, the\\n906: scan-failure test and the corpus hash set are unaffected; the lanes need\\n907: not be re-run beyond `dao.host.gate-test` itself. **How H1 and H2 clear\\n908: the tag**: H1 adds no consumer, so the nine stay tagged `:migration-source`;\\n909: H2 migrates them with the other consumers and removes them from list 1 in\\n910: the same commit, which the `list-1-equals-the-observed-arms` test enforces.\\n911: The tool lives at `src/dev/host_boundary/closure.clj` (H0's justified\\n912: deviation: the repo keeps dev tools under `src/dev/`), and the design's\\n913: earlier `dev/host_boundary/` path is read as that.\\n914: \\n915: ### 8.2 The host-library gate (H2, H3): executable references within the closure\\n916: \\n917: A literal `grep` over `src/cljc` is **not** the gate: it matches a docstring\\n918: in the untouched `dao/data.cljc:54` (\\\"a BigInt/BigDecimal\\\", V) and the\\n919: out-of-scope `dao/postgraphics/lowering.cljc:587` (`:rgba8unorm`, V), so\\n920: its asserted result would be false. The gate is instead `dao.host.gate-test`\\n921: run in **library mode**, which **lands with H2**, not H0: H0 is a freeze\\n922: with no source change and the library mode has no consumer before H2's\\n923: deletion, so building it in H0 would add a deliverable nothing exercises\\n924: and nothing can falsify; H2 builds it with the H2 name list and its two\\n925: negative tests (below), and H3 extends the name list. In library mode the\\n926: gate takes the H0 closure tool's tagged file list\\n927: for the adopted closure (so out-of-scope files never count), reads each\\n928: file with the Clojure reader per lane feature (so comments and string\\n929: literals, docstrings included, never count), and collects symbols, class\\n930: names and import/require forms; a hit is any such symbol naming\\n931: `BigInteger`, `BigDecimal`, `clojure.lang.Ratio`, `java.text`, `unorm`\\n932: (H2) or `MessageDigest`, `Blake3`, `noble`, `blake3_dart`, `package:crypto`,\\n933: `ed25519_edwards`, `goog.crypt.base64` (H3) in a file outside `dao/host/`\\n934: and, for H3's Ed25519 names, outside `yin/vm/linker/sign.cljc` (`generate`,\\n935: deferred). Codec-track files stay on list 1 and are not scanned by this\\n936: mode (their arms are the codec track's). The gate fails distinctly when the\\n937: closure list is empty or a file cannot be read, which is a scan error, not\\n938: \\\"no hits\\\".\\n939: \\n940: ### 8.3 File-disjointness from the codec track, including tests (re-checked, V)\\n941: \\n942: Codec-track source files (`codec.md` §7.1): `dao/stream/ws.cljc`,\\n943: `transit.cljc`, `cbor.cljc`, `cbor/boring.cljc`, `codec.cljc`,\\n944: `remote_channel.cljc`, `jing/stream.cljc`, `data.cljc`, the four ws adapters,\\n945: `yin/repl/{serve,connect}.cljc`. Codec-track test namespaces (`codec.md`\\n946: §7.2): the 22 requiring Transit, including `ws_test`, `ws-codec-test`,\\n947: `remote-route-test`, `loopback-net`, `transit-test`, `dao.stream.cbor-test`,\\n948: `dao.jing.stream-test`, `yin.repl.main-test`.\\n949: \\n950: H0-H4 source files: `dao/host/*` (new), `yin/vm/integer/host.cljc`,\\n951: `dao/jing/cbor.cljc`, `dao/jing/cbor/boring.cljc`, `src/cljd/dao/jing/cbor/cljd.cljd`,\\n952: `dao/jing.cljc`, `yin/vm/linker/sign.cljc`, `yin/vm/debruijn.cljc`,\\n953: `yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc`, `yin/vm/data.cljc`, `yin/vm/values.cljc`,\\n954: `yin/vm.cljc`, `yin/vm/engine.cljc`, `yin/vm/integer.cljc`,\\n955: `dao/stream/chunks.cljc`, `dao/stream/base64.cljc`, `dao/jing/dht.cljc`,\\n956: `yin/vm/linker.cljc`, `dao/stream/datagram.cljc`, `dao/data/arrays.cljc`;\\n957: and, from H0's finding (H2): `dao/space/index.cljc`, `yin/repl/query.cljc`,\\n958: `yin/vm/linker/closure.cljc`, `yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc`, `yang/php.cljc`,\\n959: `yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc`, `yin/vm/debruijn_register_effects.cljc`,\\n960: `yang/antlr/packet.cljc` (none is a codec-track file, V).\\n961: H0-H4 test files: `dao/host/*_test` (new), `yin/vm/integer_test`,\\n962: `yang/python/antlr/{int_heap,int_literal,int_ops}_test`, `dao/jing/cbor_*`,\\n963: `dao/jing_test`, `yin/vm/linker/sign_test`, `dao/stream/base64_test`,\\n964: `yin/vm/debruijn_code_test`, `yin/vm/data_test`, `dao/data/btree_*`.\\n965: \\n966: Intersection: none, with two recorded deferrals: `dao/stream/codec.cljc:45`\\n967: (`host-bytes?` over `dao.host.bytes`) after C4, and `dao/stream/cbor/boring.cljc`\\n968: (the transport writer) is **not** touched by H4. The `dao.stream.cbor-test`\\n969: and `dao.jing.cbor_test` namespaces are distinct files. The deferred H5\\n970: (§9.1) would touch `ws.cljc:122`, `ws_test.cljc:11` and\\n971: `remote_route_test.cljc:24` (V: identity-less ring creation), which is why\\n972: it is deferred behind the codec track as well as behind its own design.\\n973: \\n974: Coordination with a host-lane probe track: its \\\"narrow source adaptations\\\"\\n975: (R: the spike touched `integer/host.cljc`, `jing.cljc`, `cbor.cljc`,\\n976: `cbor/boring.cljc`) are exactly the H1-H4 files; under OQ3 that work is\\n977: paused until H4 lands and needs file-level coordination, not just a rebase.\\n978: \\n979: ## 9. DEFERRED scope (not commissionable under this document)\\n980: \\n981: The following keep their design intent from r2 but are **not commissionable\\n982: here**. They belong to a separate design, proposed name\\n983: `docs/design/dao.stream.host-effects.md`, with its own non-Claude review.\\n984: Nothing below is decided; the \\\"required inputs\\\" are the findings a\\n985: successor must answer before slices exist. Slice ids H5-H8 are reserved so\\n986: no other document's citation moves.\\n987: \\n988: ### 9.1 Entropy, identities, scheduling, ambient facts, printing (reserved H5)\\n989: \\n990: Intent: entropy as data the driver deposits (events in); identities derived\\n991: from drawn bytes and carried in creation specs; the driver owns pumping and\\n992: wake-up; ambient facts and the one core `println` as data; `gensym` with\\n993: hygienic naming. Required inputs (from the r2 review R2, R6 and §3.2):\\n994: \\n995: - exclusive allocation and resumable consumption of an entropy stream, given\\n996:   that cursors are non-destructive (`dao/stream.cljc:159-173`) and\\n997:   independent readers could reuse bytes; partial batches and loss; blocked\\n998:   resumption;\\n999: - bootstrap identities: the entropy stream itself needs an identity before\\n1000:   any byte is drawn;\\n1001: - preserved UUID spelling: `ucf/custody.cljc:50-56` requires the\\n1002:   8-4-4-4-12 lowercase form, so a derived id must keep that grammar;\\n1003: - DHT initialization draws several values synchronously\\n1004:   (`space/dht.cljc:255-269`, R): failure and continuation behaviour;\\n1005: - async completions emitted as data: moving consumer callbacks into a\\n1006:   `step!` does not remove them (R2); the `btree.storage` promise facade and\\n1007:   `content.async` consumers need a data-shaped completion;\\n1008: - the JVM blocking content driver selected at `coordinate.cljc:80`\\n1009:   (`driver.clj:169-206`: clock and sleep) is lane-specific IO inside a\\n1010:   portable composition and needs its own disposition;\\n1011: - the codec-track test edits `ws_test.cljc:11` and `remote_route_test.cljc:24`\\n1012:   and the `ws.cljc:122` site: staged compatibility or an explicit dependency\\n1013:   on C4; a re-estimate of the slice (the r2 estimate of about twenty files\\n1014:   was understated: UCF custody and holder migrations are included);\\n1015: - `gensym` hygiene: compiler counters need hygienic naming, not a reset;\\n1016:   `transact.cljc:35` tempids need separate treatment;\\n1017: - OQ9 (entropy shape: stream versus identity-in-spec with driver-minted\\n1018:   secrets; both avoid core generators, the r2 recommendation overclaimed)\\n1019:   and OQ10 (compiler `gensym`) move to that design;\\n1020: - the five `random-uuid` sites outside the transitive closure\\n1021:   (`dao/await.cljc:235,240`, `yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve.cljc:417,604,606`,\\n1022:   V, H0) and the out-of-closure `dao/jing/content/async.cljc` timer and\\n1023:   `dao/stream/udp.cljc` arms: the deferred design decides whether its scope\\n1024:   is the transitive closure (then they are out until required) or the\\n1025:   directory scope of OQ1 (then they are in).\\n1026: \\n1027: ### 9.2 The durable-storage seam (reserved H6)\\n1028: \\n1029: Intent: one seam beneath the journal with enumerated lower operations; the\\n1030: claim-file algorithm portable; capability map (`lock-kind`,\\n1031: `directory-sync?`, `failure-model`). Required inputs (R5, A7): the atomic\\n1032: replacement at `store/fs.cljc:352-387` renames **before** the directory\\n1033: sync (`:364-370`, `:382-383`, V), so a sync failure can leave the new HEAD\\n1034: visible; the seam must distinguish pre-rename failure (target unchanged),\\n1035: post-rename visibility (new HEAD visible, durability uncertain) and sync\\n1036: uncertainty, and test post-rename failure explicitly; short reads, partial\\n1037: appends, acquisition outcomes (`held`/`refused`/`unsupported`), durability\\n1038: outcomes per the declared failure model; `own-pid`, `process-alive?`,\\n1039: `create-exclusive!`, `unlink!`, `canonical-path` for the claim-file lock.\\n1040: \\n1041: ### 9.3 The parser stage (reserved H7)\\n1042: \\n1043: Intent: the grammar profile plus host walk as one seam value; a\\n1044: remote-stage test. Required input: none beyond the stage's own host walk;\\n1045: r3's \\\"one `println`\\\" at `yang/python/antlr/repl.cljc:71` was inside a\\n1046: quoted yin program (the VM's primitive, not a host call, V) and is\\n1047: withdrawn.\\n1048: \\n1049: ### 9.4 Stream-implementation conformance and the wasm import gate (reserved H8)\\n1050: \\n1051: Intent: the contract's outcome tables through a scripted seam against every\\n1052: implementation; a gate asserting a wasm binary's import list against the\\n1053: seven names. Required input: which implementations declare which outcome\\n1054: subset (`dao.stream.md`, Surfaces).\\n1055: \\n1056: ## 10. Cost and what would reverse this (H0-H4)\\n1057: \\n1058: Cost (P, from §1 and §8.3, revised r7 for H0's finding): **24 existing\\n1059: files edited** (the 16 of r5 plus the eight profile consumers H0 found:\\n1060: `dao/space/index.cljc`, `yin/repl/query.cljc`, `yin/vm/linker/closure.cljc`,\\n1061: `yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc`, `yang/php.cljc`, `yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc`,\\n1062: `yin/vm/debruijn_register_effects.cljc`, `yang/antlr/packet.cljc`; each a\\n1063: require plus one arm, so `dao.space.index` and the UCF rows file are no\"}]}],\"meta\":{\"source\":\"tool\",\"messageId\":\"29988a2c-3ad8-41b8-8dc1-c3af47c14fa5\"}},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"Continuing to read a bit further into §10 (lines 1063-1100) to confirm the correction to the claim that \\\"the index is not modified\\\" and the 3 deletions. After that, spot-check the code at about 10 locations.\\n\",\"signature\":\"\"},{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_bb2a778745de43b586614353\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md\",\"offset\":1063,\"limit\":40}},{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_04cb942b2edf4b6e9dc618d0\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"input\":{\"paths\":[\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc\",\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/php.cljc\"],\"offset\":390,\"limit\":30}}],\"meta\":{\"source\":\"model\",\"createdAt\":1792523202271,\"messageId\":\"9fabc8fb-4cc7-4332-b3aa-53d8334cd627\"}},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"tool_use_id\":\"call_bb2a778745de43b586614353\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Read 1/1 file, 40 lines\\nNote: showing lines 1063-1102. More of the file remains. Use offset=1103 to continue.\\n1063: require plus one arm, so `dao.space.index` and the UCF rows file are no\\n1064: longer \\\"untouched\\\") and **3 deleted**\\n1065: (`yin/vm/integer/host.cljc`, `dao/jing/cbor/boring.cljc`,\\n1066: `src/cljd/dao/jing/cbor/cljd.cljd`), **7** `dao.host.*` files added (five in\\n1067: H1, two in H3); **at least 5** test namespaces added (`gate-test` in H0,\\n1068: `conformance-test`, `bytes-test`, `text-test` in H1, `hash-test` in H3),\\n1069: the 3 Python integer tests and `integer_test` re-pointed; about 10^3 tests\\n1070: rerun per lane (R: JVM quick tier about 4,000); about 10^1 rewritten.\\n1071: Base64 and the Jing writer are replacements, not code motion, and are\\n1072: accepted only by their byte oracles. No performance figure is claimed; H4\\n1073: measures.\\n1074: \\n1075: Risk, revised (review N4): the laws of §2.4 and table A are **not verbatim\\n1076: extraction** in two places, and each is a behaviour change with a direct\\n1077: test: `acopy` prevalidation on JS and Dart (H2) and strict `utf8-encode`\\n1078: refusal where today's helpers substitute (H1 law, H3 consumers). The `aset`\\n1079: return value is kept as Clojure's: unchanged, stated only so the law cannot\\n1080: be read as changing it. H1 medium: new namespaces plus two new laws and\\n1081: their property tests.\\n1082: H2 medium: seventeen consumers (nine of r5 plus the eight H0 found, two of\\n1083: them with named behaviour changes, §3.1), the Jing carrier move, the arrays\\n1084: prevalidation change and the M-caller audit in one slice; mitigated by the corpus, the\\n1085: pre-deletion closure-tool gate and splitting the slice per namespace if the report\\n1086: shows drift. H3 low-to-medium: the UTF-8 behaviour change is observable only\\n1087: on unpaired-surrogate strings, which the codec already refuses. H4\\n1088: low-to-medium: the corpus decides; performance unknown until measured. The\\n1089: ClojureDart traps are named in §14.\\n1090: \\n1091: Reversal: an owner ruling that reader arms are the intended port mechanism;\\n1092: a measured H4 regression that matters (the portable writer stays as oracle\\n1093: and a host supplies a faster one behind the same profile); owner rejection\\n1094: of §12 (then §2 stands as this document's reading of the existing ABI text).\\n1095: \\n1096: ## 11. Decision record\\n1097: \\n1098: +------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+\\n1099: | Id   | Decision                                                                                                         | Status                       |\\n1100: +======+==================================================================================================================+==============================+\\n1101: | HD1  | The governing test: dao.stream wherever the contact can be an IO action with respect to the world (§2.1-2.3); an | Owner rule (\\\"test 2          |\\n1102: |      | internal pure, total, synchronous function, or a declared mutation of an owned argument, may be a direct call.   | governs\\\"); r3 wording needs  |\"}]},{\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"tool_use_id\":\"call_04cb942b2edf4b6e9dc618d0\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Read 1/1 file\\nNote: read_file output was capped at 97.7 KB. Returned 1/2 matched files; skipped 1. Use narrower patterns, or read the remaining files one at a time with offset/limit.\\nNote: offset/limit apply to a single-file read and were ignored here; every matched file is shown in full (subject to the caps above). Read one file_path at a time to window into it.\\n--- File Contents ---\\n\\n// File: src/cljc/yang/php.cljc (unknown)\\n(ns yang.php\\n  \\\"Yang PHP compiler - Compiles PHP code into Yin VM Universal AST.\\n\\n  Supports:\\n  - Function definitions (named and anonymous)\\n  - Closures with 'use' clauses\\n  - Conditionals (if/elseif/else)\\n  - Variables ($name)\\n  - Assignments ($x = val) and Augmented Assignments ($x *= val)\\n  - Post-increment ($x++)\\n  - For loops (desugared to recursive lambdas)\\n  - Basic operators and literals\\n  - Semicolon-terminated statements\\n  - Braced blocks\\n  - Type hints (parsed and ignored)\\\"\\n  (:refer-clojure :exclude [compile])\\n  (:require\\n    [clojure.string :as str]))\\n\\n\\n;; Forward declarations\\n(declare compile-stmt\\n         parse-php-expr\\n         parse-php-statement\\n         parse-php-block\\n         parse-php-primary)\\n\\n\\n;; ============================================================================\\n;; PHP Tokenizer\\n;; ============================================================================\\n\\n(defn tokenize\\n  \\\"Tokenize PHP source code.\\\"\\n  [source]\\n  (loop [s (str/trim source)\\n         tokens []]\\n    (if (empty? s)\\n      tokens\\n      (let\\n        [patterns\\n         [[:number #\\\"^\\\\d+\\\\.?\\\\d*\\\"] [:string #\\\"^\\\\\\\"([^\\\\\\\"]*)\\\\\\\"\\\"]\\n          [:string #\\\"^'([^']*)'\\\"]\\n          [:keyword\\n           #\\\"^(function|return|if|else|elseif|true|false|null|use|for|int|float|string|bool|void|mixed|array|object)\\\\b\\\"]\\n          [:variable #\\\"^\\\\$[a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*\\\"]\\n          [:identifier #\\\"^[a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*\\\"]\\n          [:operator\\n           #\\\"^(==|!=|<=|>=|<|>|\\\\+\\\\+|\\\\-\\\\-|\\\\+=|\\\\-=|\\\\*=|/=|\\\\+|-|\\\\*|/|&&|\\\\|\\\\||!|=)\\\"]\\n          [:lparen #\\\"^\\\\(\\\"] [:rparen #\\\"^\\\\)\\\"] [:lbrace #\\\"^\\\\{\\\"] [:rbrace #\\\"^\\\\}\\\"]\\n          [:comma #\\\"^,\\\"] [:semicolon #\\\"^;\\\"] [:colon #\\\"^:\\\"]\\n          [:whitespace #\\\"^[ \\\\t\\\\n\\\\r]+\\\"]]\\n         matched\\n         (some (fn [[type pattern]]\\n                 (when-let [match (re-find pattern s)]\\n                   (let [full-match (if (string? match) match (first match))\\n                         value\\n                         (if (= type :string) (second match) full-match)]\\n                     {:type type, :value value, :length (count full-match)})))\\n               patterns)]\\n        (if matched\\n          (recur (subs s (:length matched))\\n                 (if (= :whitespace (:type matched))\\n                   tokens\\n                   (conj tokens [(:type matched) (:value matched)])))\\n          (cond (str/starts-with? s \\\"<?php\\\") (recur (subs s 5) tokens)\\n                (str/starts-with? s \\\"?>\\\") (recur (subs s 2) tokens)\\n                :else (throw (ex-info \\\"Tokenization error\\\"\\n                                      {:remaining\\n                                       (subs s 0 (min 20 (count s)))}))))))))\\n\\n\\n;; ============================================================================\\n;; PHP Parser\\n;; ============================================================================\\n\\n(defn- match?\\n  [token type & [val]]\\n  (and token (= (first token) type) (or (nil? val) (= (second token) val))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- expect\\n  [tokens type & [val]]\\n  (if (match? (first tokens) type val)\\n    (rest tokens)\\n    (throw (ex-info (str \\\"Expected \\\" type \\\" \\\" (or val \\\"\\\"))\\n                    {:token (first tokens), :all (take 5 tokens)}))))\\n\\n\\n(defn parse-php-literal\\n  [[type val]]\\n  (case type\\n    :number {:php-type :literal,\\n             :value (if (str/includes? val \\\".\\\")\\n                      #?(:cljd (double/parse val)\\n                         :clj (Double/parseDouble val)\\n                         :cljs (js/parseFloat val))\\n                      #?(:cljd (int/parse val)\\n                         :clj (Long/parseLong val)\\n                         :cljs (js/parseInt val)))}\\n    :string {:php-type :literal, :value val}\\n    :keyword (case val\\n               \\\"true\\\" {:php-type :literal, :value true}\\n               \\\"false\\\" {:php-type :literal, :value false}\\n               \\\"null\\\" {:php-type :literal, :value nil}\\n               nil)\\n    nil))\\n\\n\\n(defn- skip-type-hint\\n  [tokens]\\n  (let [tok (first tokens)]\\n    (if (not tok)\\n      tokens\\n      (let [[type val] tok]\\n        (cond\\n          ;; Skip primitive type keywords\\n          (and (= :keyword type)\\n               (#{\\\"int\\\" \\\"float\\\" \\\"string\\\" \\\"bool\\\" \\\"void\\\" \\\"mixed\\\" \\\"array\\\" \\\"object\\\"}\\n                val))\\n          (rest tokens)\\n          ;; Skip identifiers that aren't keywords (likely class names)\\n          (and (= :identifier type)\\n               (not (#{\\\"function\\\" \\\"return\\\" \\\"if\\\" \\\"else\\\" \\\"elseif\\\" \\\"use\\\" \\\"for\\\"}\\n                     val))\\n               ;; Peek next: if it's a variable or closure capture, this\\n               ;; was a type hint\\n               (let [next-tok (second tokens)]\\n                 (or (= :variable (first next-tok))\\n                     (and (= :operator (first next-tok))\\n                          (= \\\"&\\\" (second next-tok))))))\\n          (rest tokens)\\n          :else tokens)))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- parse-params\\n  \\\"Parse parameter list inside parentheses.\\n   Tokens should start AFTER the opening paren.\\n   Returns {:params [names] :remaining tokens-at-rparen}\\\"\\n  [toks]\\n  (loop [params []\\n         t toks]\\n    (if (match? (first t) :rparen)\\n      {:params params, :remaining t}\\n      (let [t (skip-type-hint t)\\n            [pt pv] (first t)]\\n        (if (= :variable pt)\\n          (let [pname (symbol (subs pv 1))\\n                after-var (rest t)]\\n            (if (match? (first after-var) :comma)\\n              (recur (conj params pname) (rest after-var))\\n              (if (match? (first after-var) :rparen)\\n                {:params (conj params pname), :remaining after-var}\\n                (throw (ex-info \\\"Expected , or ) in params\\\"\\n                                {:token (first after-var)})))))\\n          (if (match? (first t) :rparen) ; Handle empty params\\n            {:params params, :remaining t}\\n            (throw (ex-info \\\"Expected param variable\\\" {:token (first t)}))))))))\\n\\n\\n(defn parse-php-primary\\n  [tokens]\\n  (let [[type val] (first tokens)]\\n    (cond\\n      (and (= :keyword type) (= \\\"function\\\" val))\\n      (let [tokens (rest tokens)\\n            tokens (expect tokens :lparen)\\n            {:keys [params remaining]} (parse-params tokens)\\n            tokens (expect remaining :rparen)\\n            ;; Optional 'use' clause\\n            {:keys [use-vars rem-after-use]}\\n            (if (match? (first tokens) :keyword \\\"use\\\")\\n              (let [after-lparen (expect (rest tokens) :lparen)\\n                    {:keys [params remaining]} (parse-params after-lparen)]\\n                {:use-vars params,\\n                 :rem-after-use (expect remaining :rparen)})\\n              {:use-vars [], :rem-after-use tokens})\\n            tokens rem-after-use\\n            ;; Optional return type\\n            tokens (if (match? (first tokens) :colon)\\n                     (skip-type-hint (rest tokens))\\n                     tokens)\\n            {:keys [ast remaining]} (parse-php-block tokens)]\\n        {:ast\\n         {:php-type :lambda, :params params, :use-vars use-vars, :body ast},\\n         :remaining remaining})\\n      (#{:number :string} type) {:ast (parse-php-literal (first tokens)),\\n                                 :remaining (rest tokens)}\\n      (and (= :keyword type) (#{\\\"true\\\" \\\"false\\\" \\\"null\\\"} val))\\n      {:ast (parse-php-literal (first tokens)), :remaining (rest tokens)}\\n      (= :variable type) {:ast {:php-type :variable,\\n                                :name (symbol (subs val 1))},\\n                          :remaining (rest tokens)}\\n      (= :identifier type) {:ast {:php-type :variable, :name (symbol val)},\\n                            :remaining (rest tokens)}\\n      (= :lparen type) (let [{:keys [ast remaining]} (parse-php-expr (rest\\n                                                                       tokens))]\\n                         {:ast ast, :remaining (expect remaining :rparen)})\\n      :else (throw (ex-info \\\"Expected primary expression\\\"\\n                            {:token (first tokens)})))))\\n\\n\\n(defn parse-php-call\\n  [tokens]\\n  (let [{:keys [ast remaining]} (parse-php-primary tokens)]\\n    (loop [current-ast ast\\n           current-rem remaining]\\n      (if (match? (first current-rem) :lparen)\\n        (let [parse-args\\n              (fn [toks]\\n                (loop [args []\\n                       t (rest toks)]\\n                  (if (match? (first t) :rparen)\\n                    {:args args, :remaining (rest t)}\\n                    (let [{:keys [ast remaining]} (parse-php-expr t)]\\n                      (if (match? (first remaining) :comma)\\n                        (recur (conj args ast) (rest remaining))\\n                        (if (match? (first remaining) :rparen)\\n                          {:args (conj args ast), :remaining (rest remaining)}\\n                          (throw (ex-info \\\"Expected , or ) in call\\\"\\n                                          {:token (first remaining)}))))))))\\n              {:keys [args remaining]} (parse-args current-rem)]\\n          (recur {:php-type :call, :function current-ast, :args args}\\n                 remaining))\\n        {:ast current-ast, :remaining current-rem}))))\\n\\n\\n(defn parse-php-unary\\n  [tokens]\\n  (let [[_type _val] (first tokens)]\\n    (cond (match? (first tokens) :operator \\\"-\\\")\\n          (let [{:keys [ast remaining]} (parse-php-unary (rest tokens))]\\n            (if (= (:php-type ast) :literal)\\n              {:ast (update ast :value -), :remaining remaining}\\n              {:ast {:php-type :binop,\\n                     :op '-,\\n                     :left {:php-type :literal, :value 0},\\n                     :right ast},\\n               :remaining remaining}))\\n          (match? (first tokens) :operator \\\"!\\\")\\n          (let [{:keys [ast remaining]} (parse-php-unary (rest tokens))]\\n            {:ast {:php-type :unaryop, :op 'not, :arg ast},\\n             :remaining remaining})\\n          :else (parse-php-call tokens))))\\n\\n\\n(defn parse-php-binary-op\\n  [tokens min-prec]\\n  (let [precedence {'* 3,\\n                    '/ 3,\\n                    '+ 2,\\n                    '- 2,\\n                    '== 1,\\n                    '!= 1,\\n                    '< 1,\\n                    '> 1,\\n                    '<= 1,\\n                    '>= 1,\\n                    '&& 0,\\n                    '|| 0}\\n        {:keys [ast remaining]} (parse-php-unary tokens)]\\n    (loop [left ast\\n           toks remaining]\\n      (let [[type val] (first toks)]\\n        (if-let [prec (and (= :operator type) (get precedence (symbol val)))]\\n          (if (>= prec min-prec)\\n            (let [{right :ast, rem :remaining} (parse-php-binary-op (rest toks)\\n                                                                    (inc prec))]\\n              (recur\\n                {:php-type :binop, :op (symbol val), :left left, :right right}\\n                rem))\\n            {:ast left, :remaining toks})\\n          {:ast left, :remaining toks})))))\\n\\n\\n(defn parse-php-expr\\n  [tokens]\\n  (let [{:keys [ast remaining]} (parse-php-binary-op tokens 0)]\\n    (cond ; Standard assignment: $x = expr\\n      (and (= :variable (:php-type ast))\\n           (match? (first remaining) :operator \\\"=\\\"))\\n      (let [{rhs :ast, rem :remaining} (parse-php-expr (rest remaining))]\\n        {:ast {:php-type :assignment, :name (:name ast), :value rhs},\\n         :remaining rem})\\n      ;; Augmented assignment: $x *= expr -> $x = $x * expr\\n      (and (= :variable (:php-type ast))\\n           (#{\\\"++\\\" \\\"--\\\" \\\"+=\\\" \\\"-=\\\" \\\"*=\\\" \\\"/=\\\"} (second (first remaining))))\\n      (let [op-str (second (first remaining))\\n            rem (rest remaining)]\\n        (cond (= op-str \\\"++\\\") {:ast {:php-type :assignment,\\n                                     :name (:name ast),\\n                                     :value {:php-type :binop,\\n                                             :op '+,\\n                                             :left ast,\\n                                             :right {:php-type :literal,\\n                                                     :value 1}}},\\n                               :remaining rem}\\n              (= op-str \\\"--\\\") {:ast {:php-type :assignment,\\n                                     :name (:name ast),\\n                                     :value {:php-type :binop,\\n                                             :op '-,\\n                                             :left ast,\\n                                             :right {:php-type :literal,\\n                                                     :value 1}}},\\n                               :remaining rem}\\n              :else\\n              (let [op (symbol (subs op-str 0 1))\\n                    {rhs :ast, rem2 :remaining} (parse-php-expr rem)]\\n                {:ast {:php-type :assignment,\\n                       :name (:name ast),\\n                       :value\\n                       {:php-type :binop, :op op, :left ast, :right rhs}},\\n                 :remaining rem2})))\\n      :else {:ast ast, :remaining remaining})))\\n\\n\\n(defn parse-php-block\\n  [tokens]\\n  (let [tokens (expect tokens :lbrace)]\\n    (loop [stmts []\\n           toks tokens]\\n      (if (match? (first toks) :rbrace)\\n        {:ast {:php-type :suite, :stmts stmts}, :remaining (rest toks)}\\n        (let [{:keys [ast remaining]} (parse-php-statement toks)]\\n          (recur (conj stmts ast) remaining))))))\\n\\n\\n(defn parse-php-for\\n  [tokens]\\n  (let [tokens (expect (rest tokens) :lparen)\\n        {init :ast, remaining :remaining} (parse-php-expr tokens)\\n        remaining (expect remaining :semicolon)\\n        {test :ast, remaining :re