{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat collab/1793740000000-engineer-p4-e2e-triage.gpt-6-luna.findings.md && sed -n '431,492p' docs/agents/build-n-test.md && cat collab/1793790000000-engineer-p4-conformance-so.gpt-6-luna.findings.md\"","aggregated_output":"# P4 e2e red triage\n\n## Bare constant refusal\n\n`constant-node` lowered unresolved unqualified constants in the global\nnamespace to `php/const-get-fq`. That moved `<?php echo FOO;` from the required\nlowering refusal into runtime undefined-constant handling, so\n`refusals-are-named-test` saw no `:yang.php/unsupported` diagnostic. The\nlowerer now refuses that global bare-name case with `:construct :constant`;\nnamespace fallback and qualified runtime lookups remain intact.\n\nFocused verification: `refusals-are-named-test`, 1 test / 22 assertions / 0\nfailures / 0 errors.\n\n## PHPT quick mismatch disposition\n\nAdded `test/yang/php/antlr/phpt_quick_mismatch_manifest.edn`. The quick\nselection test compares the exact observed failing entry IDs against the\nmanifest, checks every recorded PHPT description, validates the per-feature\ncounts, and asserts the unsupported count. GC and foreach rows name their\nengine work items. This keeps a change from silently removing or adding a\nmismatch while allowing the selection to report its known gaps honestly.\n\nAt this tree, the selected 271 entries report 108 pass, 58 unsupported, and\n105 manifested failures. The previous 115-failure / 48-unsupported report\npredates the bare-constant diagnostic fix; ten constant cases now refuse\nduring lowering. The 105 failure IDs are distributed as follows:\n\n| Feature | Count |\n| --- | ---: |\n| Zend regression cases | 70 |\n| GC cycle collection | 10 |\n| Foreach mutation/reference semantics | 11 |\n| Named parameter binding | 3 |\n| Unset CV behavior | 4 |\n| Array references | 1 |\n| Pass by reference | 5 |\n| Array internal pointer | 1 |\n\n## Thrown error\n\nThe requested quick namespace rerun completed without a thrown test error:\n20 tests / 1,116 assertions / 0 failures / 0 errors. The earlier single error\nwas not reproduced at this tip; this clean run does not identify its original\nstack. The PHPT worker catches engine throws and classifies them as entry\nfailures, so the prior error was outside that per-entry catch.\n\n## `gc_013` oracle cross-check\n\nThe pinned row is `Zend/tests/gc_013.phpt`; source builds 10,001 self-reference\ncycles, then prints the result of `gc_collect_cycles() > 0` followed by `ok`.\nThe pinned expectation is `bool(true)\\nok`. `phpt/matches-expect?` trims\ntrailing whitespace and compares the actual body, so the recorded source and\ncomparison shape are consistent on inspection.\n\nOn shiva, ran the exact pinned source through `docker run --rm -i\nphp:8.3.35-cli` under `timeout 300`. The real oracle printed:\n\n```text\nbool(true)\nok\n```\n\nThis matches the recorded pin exactly. The local engine stress test completed\nin about six minutes with\n`{:out \"\", :diag [], :uncaught {:class \"Error\", :message \"Call to undefined function gc_collect_cycles()\"}}`.\nThe three-way result is therefore:\n\n| Source | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Pinned `phpt_selection.edn` | `bool(true)\\nok` |\n| Docker PHP 8.3.35 on shiva | `bool(true)` then `ok`; matches pin |\n| Engine | Empty output, then uncaught `Error: Call to undefined function gc_collect_cycles()` |\n\nAdded this as `:slow-known-gaps` in the mismatch manifest, with the oracle pin,\nengine result, and named GC work item. The slow PHPT stress test checks this\nrecorded result explicitly. Proposed gap wording: **“PHP cyclic garbage\ncollection is not implemented; `gc_013` self-referential cycles are not\ncollected, so `gc_collect_cycles()` does not return a positive cycle count.”**\n\n## Verification\n\n- PHP e2e quick namespace: 20 tests / 1,116 assertions / 0 failures / 0 errors.\n- PHPT quick manifest test after adding the slow `gc_013` known-gap row: 1\n  test / 5 assertions / 0 failures / 0 errors (271 entries: 108 pass, 58\n  unsupported, 105 manifested failures).\n- `gc_013` engine stress test: one expected known-gap mismatch with the exact\n  recorded engine result above; its slow test now asserts that result and the\n  pinned oracle text.\n- `cljstyle check` on the changed Clojure files: clean.\n- clj-kondo on the changed Clojure files: 0 errors, 0 warnings.\n- `git diff --check`: clean.\n- PHP literal/runtime, class model, include, lower-portable, and scope consumers:\n  46 tests / 1,975 assertions / 0 failures / 0 errors.\n- The full `bb test:sub:clj yang.php` attempt was stopped after 13 minutes\n  without a summary in e2e; the standalone e2e gate and focused consumers above\n  completed successfully.\n\n## Commits\n\n- `6dee9f26 test(yang.php): record PHPT quick mismatch manifest`\n- `bf8c9c20 fix(yang.php): refuse unresolved global constants`\n\nBoth commits are on `yang-php-p4`; neither was pushed. This findings file is\nuncommitted as requested.\n## Remote test servers: shiva and jupiter\n\nTwo Linux x86_64 servers run the full suite faster than a laptop. Both are\nreached over SSH as `sto` with key authentication, and both have `mise`, `tmux`\nand `git`.\n\n| Host | Cores / RAM | Toolchain state (server snapshot checked 2026-10-11; repo selection comes from `mise.toml`) |\n|---|---|---|\n| `shiva.stigmergy.systems` | 24 / 62 GB | Server snapshot: java 21, clojure 1.12.4.1602, node 25.6.1, babashka, cljstyle, zprint, flutter 3.47.1. The repo's `mise.toml` selects Flutter `latest` on beta, not a fixed version. Activate the repo toolchain before running any lane. |\n| `jupiter.stigmergy.systems` | 48 / 62 GB | Server snapshot (rechecked 2026-10-29): java 21, clojure 1.12.4.1602, node 25.6.1, babashka, cljstyle, zprint, flutter 3.47.8 (the stale hand-symlinked 3.41.9 was replaced via `mise install flutter@3.47.8` after it failed to compile `dart:ui`-using cljd namespaces; if the Dart lane dies in the cljd compile, check `mise ls flutter` first). Tri-host quick tier verified green on 2026-10-29 (see Measured times). |\n\n**Never test in `~/workspace/datomworld` on either host.** It is a working copy\nthat is behind origin (shiva: 45 commits behind on 2026-10-11) and belongs to its\nowner. Use a scratch clone under `~/ci/` and leave the working copy alone.\n\n### Get the code there: push to origin, never rsync\n\nRsyncing a worktree over the WAN ran at about 150 KB/s (576 MB of tracked files\nwould take about an hour), and an unanchored `--exclude build` also dropped source\ndirectories named `build`, `out` and `target`. Both hosts reach GitHub, so push the\nbranch from the laptop (a feature branch, never master), make one scratch clone on\nthe host from its existing checkout (a local clone takes seconds), and fetch:\n\n```sh\n# once per host: a separate scratch clone, not the working copy\nssh shiva.stigmergy.systems 'set -e; mkdir -p ~/ci; cd ~/workspace/datomworld;\n  URL=$(git remote get-url origin);\n  git clone -q --no-checkout ~/workspace/datomworld ~/ci/datomworld-<name>;\n  cd ~/ci/datomworld-<name>; git remote set-url origin \"$URL\";\n  git fetch -q origin; git checkout -q --detach origin/<branch>'\n```\n\nTo test another branch later, fetch and check it out in the scratch clone with\n`git fetch origin` then `git checkout --detach origin/<branch>`. A branch that\nwas never pushed cannot be tested remotely.\n\n### Activate the toolchain in the right order\n\nA non-interactive `ssh host cmd` does not load the shell profile, so `mise` and its\ntools are not on PATH. In a script, do this in exactly this order, after the `cd`\ninto the clone:\n\n```sh\nexport PATH=\"$HOME/.local/bin:/snap/bin:$PATH\"   # mise: ~/.local/bin on shiva, /snap/bin on jupiter\ncd ~/ci/datomworld-<name>\nmise trust >/dev/null 2>&1                       # trust is per path; a fresh clone is untrusted\nmise install                                    # install versions selected by this checkout's mise.toml\neval \"$(mise env -s bash)\"                       # puts the repo-selected tools on PATH\nmise current flutter                            # verify the selected Flutter version\n```\n\nActivating mise before the `cd` and `mise trust` leaves the repo-selected tools\n(flutter in particular) off PATH: the Dart lane then dies in seconds with \"Can't\nfind flutter on PATH\", and so does `bb build:yin-repl-peer`.\n\n### Which lanes may overlap (reconciling the one-lane-set rule)\n\n\"One lane set at a time\" and \"one Dart lane at a time\" are per-machine rules about\nCPU: they exist because a laptop has 8 cores. They are not a rule about repos.\n`test.subsystems.md` section 5 item 6 says the same (\"on one machine where\navoidable\"). On shiva (24 cores) and jupiter (48) the cores are not the limit, so\nlanes may overlap, with these limits:\n# P4 conformance stack overflow findings\n\n## Reproduction\n\nThe focused export conformance test reproduces on a reduced stack with:\n\n```sh\nclojure -J-Xss512k -M:test -n yang.php.antlr.e2e-test \\\n  -v yang.php.antlr.e2e-test/real-lowered-ts-export-called-from-php-test\n```\n\nThe first failure was in `yang.tails/mark-tails`. After replacing the test's\nwhole-tree `postwalk` used to find `php/run-main` with an identity-aware path\nlookup, the failure moved to `yin.vm/ast->datoms-with-root` while converting\nthe composed caller AST. The failure remains with the TS donor source reduced\nto a direct arrow expression and with only its `js/make-function` node selected.\n\n## Root cause and fix\n\nThe original harness evaluated the TS donor as an operand nested inside the\nPHP caller AST. The donor source assigns its function to `globalThis`, so\nlowering that assignment brings the donor program's shared global publication\nstructure into the AST being walked for the caller. This is a composition\nerror; it is not a defect in published-export reference lowering.\n\nThe harness now evaluates the lowered donor program to completion first. That\npublishes the function cell in the VM's global table. A separate PHP AST then\nreads the named cell with `js/global-get` and projects that runtime value into\nthe PHP function or global namespace before executing the unchanged PHP\nsource. The donor AST is never nested in the caller AST. The helper locates\n`php/run-main` with identity-aware traversal, avoiding a full `postwalk` over\nshared lowered subtrees.\n\nThe focused export test and all three `real-lowered-*` tests pass at the\ndefault JVM stack. The `-J-Xss512k` focused run advances past the former walk\noverflow but still overflows later in VM datom-to-AST reconstruction during\nexecution; that is separate from the former non-terminating composition walk.\n`yang.cross-lang-test` also passes at default stack (3 tests, 5 assertions).\nThe full `bb test:sub:clj yang.php` lane was started but interrupted after it\nremained in the broad PHP e2e namespace without progress output. Kondo,\ncljstyle and `git diff --check` pass for the changed test file. No full-lane\ngreen result is claimed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
